        "original_id": "2e9c41e0-a703-53de-9501-8a6089335549",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Welbeck Hill, Laceby, Riby, River Freshney, North East Lincolnshire, Lincolnshire Wolds, England, Wellington\n- People: Harold Temple White\n- Topics: Archaeology, local folklore, geography\n\nFacts:\n- Welbeck Hill is an archaeological site with Roman and early Saxon pottery finds and an Anglo-Saxon cemetery in North East Lincolnshire, England.\n- Welbeck Hill is located about 1.75 miles from Laceby and about 3 miles from Riby.\n- Laceby is a village and civil parish in North East Lincolnshire, England.\n- River Freshney rises from at least four springs on the edge of the Lincolnshire Wolds.\n- Local folklore and oral tradition say that River Freshney springs from Welbeck Hill.\n- Harold Temple White was born in Laceby, Lincolnshire, England, in 1881.\n- Harold Temple White resided in Wellington for much of his life.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f4dc8ee9-6fc0-54e0-a0c3-d1dfce41c706",
        "text": "Page: Welbeck Hill. Sentence: Welbeck Hill is the site of Roman and early Saxon pottery finds, and an Anglo-Saxon cemetery, located around 1.75 miles from Laceby, and around 3 miles from Riby, in North East Lincolnshire, England.\nPage: Laceby. Sentence: Laceby is a village and civil parish in North East Lincolnshire, England.\nPage: River Freshney. Sentence: It rises from at least four springs on the edge of the Lincolnshire Wolds, although local folklore and oral tradition has it springing from Welbeck Hill.\nPage: Harold Temple White. Sentence: He was born in Laceby, Lincolnshire, England, in 1881, and resided in Wellington for much of his life.",
